[SIZE=6][B]MC Data Bridge - Release Notes (v2.2.0)[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Overview[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Version 2.2.0 introduces [B]Map Sync Between Servers[/B], allowing player-held map items ([CODE]Material.FILLED_MAP[/CODE]) to be stashed and restored per-server across proxy networks without map canvas corruption or ID conflicts, alongside core dependency updates.[/SIZE]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Key Changes[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]🗺️ Map Sync Between Servers (#36)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Server-Isolated Map Stashing ([CODE]mode: return[/CODE]):[/B] Filled map items created on Server A are tagged with origin metadata ([CODE]databridge:origin_server[/CODE] and [CODE]databridge:original_map_id[/CODE]). When transferring to Server B, foreign maps are safely stashed in the database ([CODE]databridge_maps[/CODE]) and automatically restored to their inventory slots when returning to Server A.
[*][B]Configurable Map Synchronization Modes:[/B] Added a new [CODE]maps:[/CODE] config section supporting three modes:
[LIST]
[*][CODE]return[/CODE] (default): Stashes and restores server-specific map items per server.
[*][CODE]global[/CODE]: Synchronizes map canvas pixel data across all network servers.
[*][CODE]untracked[/CODE]: Legacy vanilla map handling.
[/LIST]
[*][B]Component Database Storage:[/B] Added [CODE]{table-prefix}databridge_maps[/CODE] table in MySQL and SQLite for atomic map persistence and cross-server UUID data migration.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]📦 Dependency Updates[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]MySQL Connector/J:[/B] Updated [CODE]com.mysql:mysql-connector-j[/CODE] from [CODE]9.7.0[/CODE] to [CODE]26.7.0[/CODE].
[*][B]Item NBT API:[/B] Updated [CODE]de.tr7zw:item-nbt-api[/CODE] from [CODE]2.15.7[/CODE] to [CODE]2.16.0[/CODE].
[*][B]JUnit Jupiter:[/B] Updated [CODE]org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter[/CODE] from [CODE]6.1.0[/CODE] to [CODE]6.1.3[/CODE].
[/LIST]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]
[I]For installation instructions and configuration details, please refer to the README.md and config.yml.[/I]
